For sets $A_1, A_2, A_3, ...$ the operations extend to $inter.big_(n=1)^oo A_n = {x: x in A_n forall n in NN}$ and $union.big_(n=1)^oo A_n = {x: x in A_n exists n in NN}$. More generally, for a collection $(A_i)_(i in I)$ indexed by a set $I$, $inter.big_(i in I) A_i = {x: x in A_i forall i in I}$ and $union.big_(i in I) A_i = {x: x in A_i exists i in I}$. The symbol $oo$ here records the index set $NN$; it does not mean the limit of anything.
